## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of multi-region AWS deployments using Terraform provider aliases and proper resource binding to specific providers.

## Key Concepts
- Terraform provider aliases for multiple AWS regions
- Resource addressing with provider assignments
- Cross-region planning and deployment validation

## Code Example
```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

provider "aws" {
  alias  = "west"
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_vpc" "east_vpc" {
  cidr_block = "10.0.0.0/16"
}

resource "aws_nat_gateway" "west_nat" {
  provider     = aws.west
  allocation_id = aws_eip.nat_eip.id
  subnet_id    = aws_subnet.west_subnet.id
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to implement policy-based gating and cross-account state references in production workflows.

## Key Concepts
- Terraform Cloud and Sentinel policy gating
- remote_state across AWS accounts
- per-environment workspaces (qa/prod)
- CI integration for plan upload and gate checks

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal Sentinel-like policy (illustrative)
import "tfplan/v2"
import "strings"

let prodChange = false
for (rc in tfplan.resource_changes) {
  if (strings.contains(rc.address, ".prod.")) {
    if (rc.change.actions.includes("create") || rc.change.actions.includes("update") || rc.change.actions.includes("delete")) {
      prodChange = true
    }
  }
}
function main() { return !prodChange }
```

